eir own saints at traditionally Christian places of worship.”  “Certainly the order [Bektashi] was heterodox and more than any other served as a refuge for dissidents fleeing persecution. As a result, Hurufis, in addition to Shi’ites and especially Kizilbas, have left traces of their ideas in the doctrine of the order, syncretistic to a fault. But, even so, the Bektasis remained licit and, as is well known, had considerable influence among the janissaries.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1972, 'temperature': 0.2})
