uo1974, 1362–63). But filial piety was one of the core values of Confucianism and was incompatible with Buddhist thought. This suggests that a programme of Buddhist building sponsored by the royal court could be oriented towards the remaking of Buddhism in the formation of imperial ideology that was not the result of a process of systematic, coherent and abstract reasoning but contained a congeries of diffused sources, sometimes even contradictory, for practical political needs." '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1837, 'temperature': 0.2})
